WEBVTT

00:22.480 --> 00:23.940
What was that?

00:24.691 --> 00:27.152
It's unlike any of the usual
Divine Artifacts we've seen.

00:34.534 --> 00:36.036
Listen, fighters.

00:37.120 --> 00:39.122
Your bosses are no longer alive.

00:39.914 --> 00:43.793
You have two choices.

00:46.004 --> 00:48.423
Either we continue fighting

00:48.506 --> 00:50.467
until one of us falls,

00:50.550 --> 00:54.888
or we make a deal and you join us.

00:55.472 --> 00:56.973
As humans and monsters,

00:57.057 --> 00:59.684
why don't we work hand-in-hand
to co-exist?

01:03.855 --> 01:04.856
Huh?

01:04.939 --> 01:06.024
Please, wait for me!

01:16.868 --> 01:19.079
Do you know that monster?

01:19.537 --> 01:21.164
I'm sorry for your loss.

01:23.124 --> 01:24.542
Just what are you saying...

01:24.626 --> 01:27.295
You monsters have no chance of winning.

01:29.380 --> 01:32.050
Please stop any evildoings
you may be planning.

01:32.133 --> 01:33.134
What?

01:38.765 --> 01:40.433
Go! Go! Loser Ranger!

03:04.642 --> 03:08.897
Episode 3
Our Evil Will Bloom, Someday

03:08.980 --> 03:10.899
You... How did you find out--

03:10.982 --> 03:15.403
Just now, I was hiding and overheard
your conversation with Suzukiri.

03:20.116 --> 03:21.618
Please give up.

03:24.621 --> 03:28.750
Even if we continue to fight,
justice will always prevail.

03:31.628 --> 03:33.338
Justice, you say?

03:33.755 --> 03:38.301
For the past 12 years, we've been forced
to play along with your charade!

03:38.384 --> 03:40.428
I'm sick of that!

03:40.511 --> 03:43.556
I'll put an end
to that messed-up organization!

03:44.140 --> 03:47.101
Because I'm a monster!

03:52.774 --> 03:54.234
You pass!

03:54.317 --> 03:55.485
What?

03:55.568 --> 03:57.487
You passed the recruitment exam!

03:57.570 --> 03:59.072
From today onwards,

03:59.155 --> 04:01.157
you'll join us as a fellow Ranger!

04:01.241 --> 04:03.493
"Fellow Ranger"?
What are you saying at a time like this...

04:03.576 --> 04:06.829
This world is imperfect.
It's normal to be dissatisfied with it!

04:06.913 --> 04:09.874
In that case, we can change it
from within, fair and square!

04:09.958 --> 04:11.376
Let's work together

04:11.459 --> 04:14.504
to create a society
where humans and monsters can co-exist!

04:14.587 --> 04:15.588
Please!

04:17.757 --> 04:19.592
I hate you.

04:21.678 --> 04:23.846
You and I are enemies.

04:23.930 --> 04:26.391
Never talk to me again.

04:28.434 --> 04:32.438
You aren't fit to be a Ranger.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.032
<i>I believed in you.</i>

04:43.366 --> 04:45.994
I knew you'd come to me.

04:48.079 --> 04:49.747
Don't get the wrong idea.

04:50.373 --> 04:53.501
I'm just here to learn
how to defeat the Rangers.

04:54.002 --> 04:56.421
Once I'm done with you,
I'm cutting you off.

04:56.504 --> 04:59.173
Sorry that I'm a monster.

04:59.757 --> 05:01.134
How cheeky.

05:07.682 --> 05:10.518
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

05:10.601 --> 05:13.855
I see... So that's how you use mimicry
to turn into a human.

05:13.938 --> 05:16.024
Are you stupid? What are you thinking?

05:16.733 --> 05:19.027
I'm sure
people are going to be so surprised

05:19.110 --> 05:22.030
if they know that a monster
is walking around in the streets.

05:23.614 --> 05:26.534
You understand your situation now?

05:26.617 --> 05:28.286
Tsk.

05:29.078 --> 05:30.121
So...

05:30.621 --> 05:34.542
you want to know
how to defeat the Rangers, right?

05:35.626 --> 05:37.879
The key lies in the Divine Artifacts.

05:39.380 --> 05:41.382
<i>There are five different Divine Artifacts.</i>

05:41.466 --> 05:44.385
<i>They're transformation items
for the Dragon Keepers,</i>

05:44.469 --> 05:46.721
<i>created to fight monsters.</i>

05:46.804 --> 05:51.809
They're also cheat items
that grant the user divine powers.

05:52.769 --> 05:56.022
Divine Artifacts are capable of killing
the immortal monsters.

05:56.105 --> 05:57.231
In other words...

05:57.315 --> 06:00.526
You plan to do something
to those Divine Artifacts?

06:00.610 --> 06:02.028
Bingo.

06:02.737 --> 06:06.908
<i>The Ranger Force may appear
to be very powerful, but in truth,</i>

06:06.991 --> 06:09.660
<i>it's an incomplete organization that
relies heavily on the top five members.</i>

06:10.328 --> 06:12.663
<i>If we just poke
at where they're imbalanced,</i>

06:12.747 --> 06:15.249
<i>it might crumble easier than we expect.</i>

06:16.542 --> 06:19.128
Still... if it's that important,

06:19.212 --> 06:22.131
they'd never take their eyes away from it,
would they?

06:22.215 --> 06:24.258
You plan to strike
while they're asleep or something?

06:27.637 --> 06:29.305
That's one way,

06:29.889 --> 06:31.099
but there's a specific moment

06:31.182 --> 06:34.060
when they'd have to leave
their Divine Artifacts.

06:36.896 --> 06:39.607
And that's the Sunday Showdown.

06:40.274 --> 06:44.487
<i>They can't bring the real ones
to a fake battle, after all.</i>

06:44.570 --> 06:46.739
<i>This is the time you've been waiting for,</i>

06:46.823 --> 06:48.449
<i>Ranger fans all across the nation!</i>

06:48.533 --> 06:51.119
<i>It's finally time
for the usual Sunday Showdown!</i>

06:54.205 --> 06:57.250
Wow, you're looking
more like Red by the minute.

06:57.333 --> 06:59.168
If fighters are capable
of things like these,

06:59.252 --> 07:01.295
we can't afford to underestimate you guys.

07:01.838 --> 07:04.173
Shut up.
Could you not talk to me?

07:04.257 --> 07:06.217
I need more focus for unfamiliar faces.

07:06.717 --> 07:09.429
Hey. If you guys are good
at mimicking humans,

07:09.512 --> 07:11.681
why didn't you use it to your advantage?

07:11.764 --> 07:14.100
You could blend in
and do spy activities or something.

07:14.600 --> 07:17.395
There are things
we're good at mimicking and bad at.

07:17.478 --> 07:18.479
I see...

07:19.647 --> 07:20.898
You're taking too long.

07:21.482 --> 07:24.610
I'm getting tired,
so transform into a chair for now.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.239
You're seriously annoying me!

07:29.323 --> 07:33.244
I just happen to be good
at mimicking surface-dwellers.

07:33.786 --> 07:34.787
Is that so?

07:35.455 --> 07:40.126
But this special skill of yours
could change the tide of the battle.

07:49.302 --> 07:51.179
I'm in.
<i>Okay.</i>

07:51.262 --> 07:52.972
<i>The signal's good.</i>

07:53.055 --> 07:55.975
<i>All right, Fighter-kun,
go steal the Divine Artifact.</i>

07:56.058 --> 07:57.685
<i>And don't blow your cover!</i>

07:57.768 --> 08:00.438
<i>This girl...
She talks as if it's none of her business...</i>

08:00.521 --> 08:02.523
<i>There should be a staircase at the end,</i>

08:02.607 --> 08:04.358
<i>at the far right
of the passageway you're facing.</i>

08:04.442 --> 08:06.277
It's so dark, I can't see anything.

08:06.360 --> 08:07.987
How do you know that?

08:08.070 --> 08:10.239
<i>I guess
you could call it a woman's intuition.</i>

08:10.323 --> 08:12.950
<i>She always avoids answering
important questions...</i>

08:13.493 --> 08:17.079
Suzukiri... you're with the Rangers, right?

08:17.163 --> 08:19.081
Why are you helping a monster?

08:19.624 --> 08:21.334
<i>You ever watched teenage dramas?</i>

08:21.417 --> 08:22.418
What?

08:22.502 --> 08:27.048
<i>The trope is to get a dull girl
and the hottest guy in school together.</i>

08:27.131 --> 08:31.219
<i>Other girls or guys may appear as rivals
as the story progresses,</i>

08:31.302 --> 08:34.805
<i>but the original couple
will always end up together.</i>

08:34.889 --> 08:36.557
What are you talking about?

08:36.641 --> 08:38.809
<i>I feel bad for the rivals.</i>

08:38.893 --> 08:41.395
The main characters always win in the end,

08:41.479 --> 08:43.314
so I just can't bring myself
to cheer for them.

08:43.397 --> 08:45.775
That's why
I want to help you, Fighter-kun.

08:54.283 --> 08:56.786
<i>They can't tell
I'm an imposter. I can do this!</i>

08:58.579 --> 08:59.789
<i>Are you listening?</i>

09:00.665 --> 09:01.666
Stare...

09:02.917 --> 09:03.918
I see stairs.

09:04.001 --> 09:05.002
<i>That's it.</i>

09:05.086 --> 09:07.171
<i>Go down and you'll find
where they keep the Divine Artifact.</i>

09:12.718 --> 09:14.929
You're back already, Red?

09:17.014 --> 09:18.182
Yeah.

09:18.266 --> 09:19.934
<i>I can't chicken out now.</i>

09:24.689 --> 09:27.024
<i>I'm done running away!</i>

09:29.485 --> 09:32.196
I need to use the Divine Artifact
to transform again.

09:32.280 --> 09:33.864
I'm going in.

09:34.448 --> 09:35.741
Sure, go ahead.

09:46.794 --> 09:48.296
Still, Red...

09:48.379 --> 09:52.174
I'm impressed that you're willing to deal
with those trash mobs every week.

09:52.258 --> 09:54.010
<i>Calm down.</i>

09:54.093 --> 09:55.928
<i>Don't forget your objective.</i>

09:58.264 --> 10:00.182
They may be weak, but they're monsters.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.892
We can't underestimate them.

10:02.852 --> 10:05.438
Must be tough being the Red Keeper.

10:06.063 --> 10:10.818
Whatever. I don't care so long as I have
a justified reason to kill monsters.

10:10.901 --> 10:12.570
Right.

10:12.653 --> 10:14.572
I hope you guys keep up that attitude.

10:19.577 --> 10:20.578
Huh...

10:21.162 --> 10:23.914
<i>You endured well. Good job.</i>

10:28.044 --> 10:31.213
All right. Let's see
where he hid the Divine Artifact...

10:35.217 --> 10:38.137
<i>No way...
He just left it out in the open?</i>

10:38.220 --> 10:40.723
<i>This ain't some home decor.
Isn't this too careless?</i>

10:41.223 --> 10:42.767
<i>Is this a trap?</i>

10:42.850 --> 10:43.976
<i>Probably not.</i>

10:44.060 --> 10:45.311
<i>This must be what Suzukiri meant</i>

10:45.394 --> 10:47.146
<i>when she said
that the Rangers are incomplete.</i>

10:47.229 --> 10:51.150
<i>That guy doesn't even think of us
as threats.</i>

10:51.734 --> 10:54.528
<i>How dare you look down on us.
You'll be sorry!</i>

10:57.365 --> 10:58.532
<i>I got it!</i>

10:58.949 --> 11:01.285
<i>I finally got my hands on the very thing</i>

11:01.369 --> 11:02.703
<i>that's been tormenting us for years...</i>

11:06.165 --> 11:09.710
Oh, come on! I thought
you smelled different from usual.

11:09.794 --> 11:11.962
So you're an impostor!

11:12.046 --> 11:13.422
Smell?

11:13.506 --> 11:16.467
What if it was the real Red?
He would've died!

11:16.550 --> 11:17.968
Are you stupid?

11:18.052 --> 11:22.223
The real Red would never fall
for a surprise attack like that!

11:22.306 --> 11:24.517
Fine. Since my cover's blown,
I have no choice.

11:24.600 --> 11:27.687
But just try to attack me. If you do--

11:29.063 --> 11:31.107
Huh? Come again?

11:31.190 --> 11:32.191
I said--

11:32.942 --> 11:33.943
Stop--

11:34.026 --> 11:36.320
What'll happen to me if I shoot you?

11:38.197 --> 11:39.615
I said-- Wait--

11:39.699 --> 11:41.617
You guys creep me out
with how you keep regenerating.

11:41.701 --> 11:45.037
Don't act so cocky
just because you don't die!

11:45.121 --> 11:47.581
You guys probably think
you'll win one day.

11:47.665 --> 11:49.875
That's why you'll always be weak!

11:53.337 --> 11:57.800
We humans die one day,
so the fear of death makes us grow!

12:14.817 --> 12:16.569
I did a good deed yet again today!

12:17.153 --> 12:19.280
This is why I can't stop killing monsters!

12:20.656 --> 12:22.575
Let's end this now, shall we?

12:22.658 --> 12:25.077
D-Damn you...

12:25.161 --> 12:28.247
I've always wanted to try using this.

12:28.330 --> 12:30.082
Y-You can use it?
- What?

12:30.166 --> 12:32.084
Anyone other than the Dragon Keepers
can use it?

12:32.168 --> 12:34.420
Well, it'll be my first time trying.

12:34.503 --> 12:35.921
I'll test it on you.

12:36.422 --> 12:38.841
Let's see if it really can kill
an immortal monster.

12:38.924 --> 12:40.259
W-Wait!

12:40.342 --> 12:41.844
I don't want to die!

12:41.927 --> 12:44.513
Why's a monster like you having regrets
like a normal human?

12:44.972 --> 12:46.348
Is that all for your final words?

12:46.432 --> 12:47.850
No, I've got more!

12:47.933 --> 12:50.603
Ugh... What else?

12:53.063 --> 12:56.025
What? Come on... Isn't that a dynamite?

12:56.108 --> 12:57.276
That's right!

12:57.359 --> 13:00.279
Damn you! You should've said that first!

13:00.362 --> 13:03.532
Shut up!
That's what I've been trying to say!

13:03.616 --> 13:07.787
Listen! Just try attacking me,
and the entire place is going to blow up!

13:09.747 --> 13:12.208
W-Wait, let's not be too hasty, okay?

13:13.542 --> 13:15.920
Why don't we have a heart-to-heart talk?

13:16.003 --> 13:17.379
No need to play dirty...

13:17.463 --> 13:20.800
Come on,
you could remember once in a while.

13:20.883 --> 13:22.301
We monsters came here

13:22.384 --> 13:24.220
to achieve world domination.

13:24.303 --> 13:27.973
Here you go. It's the fear of death
that you like so much.

13:28.057 --> 13:31.143
D-Don't do it!

13:36.440 --> 13:37.983
You... little...

13:38.818 --> 13:42.154
Unlike you guys,
I can't afford to act cool!

13:42.238 --> 13:43.948
Don't blame me!

13:46.033 --> 13:48.452
<i>Not bad.
You're stronger than I expected.</i>

13:48.953 --> 13:49.954
<i>You did really well.</i>

13:50.329 --> 13:52.331
<i>I'm glad I came to you for the job.</i>

13:52.832 --> 13:53.874
<i>I'm sure you'll...</i>

13:53.958 --> 13:55.835
S-Stop praising me, will you?

13:56.377 --> 13:58.212
<i>Damn.
I managed to win for once,</i>

13:58.295 --> 14:00.005
<i>but I feel so irritated for some reason.</i>

14:00.089 --> 14:02.132
All right.
I reached the rooftop as planned.

14:04.093 --> 14:06.637
<i>Nice one!
Maybe I should reward you.</i>

14:06.720 --> 14:09.640
What? I don't need a reward...

14:10.641 --> 14:11.892
<i>Fighter-kun?</i>

14:12.726 --> 14:16.397
Oh, my bad. Can we talk later?

14:16.480 --> 14:18.941
I'm kind of busy right now.

14:19.733 --> 14:22.903
Why are you here?
Don't you need to deal with the monsters?

14:23.487 --> 14:26.156
No problem. There's one in front of me.

14:31.579 --> 14:32.580
All right, monster.

14:33.289 --> 14:35.457
Return the Divine Artifact
to me right now and disappear.

14:35.541 --> 14:38.210
You're the one that's going to disappear,
Red Keeper!

14:45.509 --> 14:47.803
Stop trying to show off!

14:58.105 --> 15:00.024
Ugh... I'm not done yet!

15:00.107 --> 15:02.568
Oh my... Where did your arm go?

15:03.277 --> 15:07.197
Don't worry, I'm going to put it back on,
together with what it's on!

15:19.293 --> 15:20.961
The power of regeneration, huh?

15:25.132 --> 15:27.092
Reminds me of the time
I was in the baseball club.

15:29.094 --> 15:30.679
That's a meatball!

15:33.766 --> 15:34.850
Homerun!

15:35.351 --> 15:36.685
He did that with just a pipe?

15:44.026 --> 15:47.738
No! My arm! And the Divine Artifact!

15:57.748 --> 15:58.916
Hey.

15:58.999 --> 16:01.919
You made me drop my left arm!

16:02.002 --> 16:05.923
Oh? Is my Divine Artifact
more important than your own arm?

16:06.507 --> 16:09.176
Good job.
I'm touched by your efforts.

16:09.593 --> 16:12.179
- But you look unsightly.
- What?

16:12.262 --> 16:14.181
I'd say you're not up for the task.

16:14.848 --> 16:17.267
This isn't even enough
to make a stage for you villains.

16:17.893 --> 16:18.936
You're nothing but a loser.

16:19.853 --> 16:24.024
Huh? I'd say I'm doing pretty well
for a weak fighter!

16:24.108 --> 16:26.360
This is my full power!

16:26.443 --> 16:28.862
So don't you hold back too!

16:35.119 --> 16:40.499
Don't be conceited. Why would I defeat
a mere fighter when there's no audience?

16:40.582 --> 16:43.752
Just think about your role in all of this.

16:47.589 --> 16:50.718
Red Keeper is right here!

16:50.801 --> 16:53.804
He chased down a fighter
that escaped from the arena!

16:53.887 --> 16:55.973
A fight's going down outside of the arena!

16:56.056 --> 16:59.226
And now's the time I go all out. Get it?

16:59.309 --> 17:02.604
<i>Tens of thousands of people
in front of the TV</i>

17:02.688 --> 17:04.690
<i>are excited to see you lose.</i>

17:05.274 --> 17:10.446
<i>They're waiting to see you
die pathetically as your limbs scatter.</i>

17:10.529 --> 17:12.698
You've been living in disgrace
this whole time.

17:12.781 --> 17:15.701
You can at least do the world a favor
when you die.

17:15.784 --> 17:18.412
Just when will you stop ridiculing us?

17:18.871 --> 17:21.707
Watch me shock the crowd
when they see a weak fighter

17:21.790 --> 17:23.959
defeat the leader of the Rangers!

17:24.043 --> 17:25.711
Uh?

17:27.296 --> 17:31.592
Oh, no! The injury I got
from the tiger monster last week...

17:31.675 --> 17:33.218
<i>What's up with him suddenly?</i>

17:33.302 --> 17:34.720
<i>But if he isn't acting...</i>

17:34.803 --> 17:38.223
Small fry.
You think you can fight me one-on-one?

17:38.807 --> 17:40.059
Oh, I almost forgot.

17:40.142 --> 17:41.727
What? Blue--

17:47.357 --> 17:49.276
What are you doing, Red?

17:50.444 --> 17:52.446
Well... I was acting.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.198
Cameras!

17:54.573 --> 17:56.158
Don't be mistaken, monster!

17:57.201 --> 17:58.827
We're just protecting!

17:59.328 --> 18:02.372
Together with my comrades,
we're protecting everyone on this planet!

18:02.456 --> 18:05.876
Well said!
This is going to be a legendary battle!

18:05.959 --> 18:08.879
If you don't like that,
then don't invade us!

18:08.962 --> 18:11.632
The heck?
What the hell are you talking about?

18:11.715 --> 18:13.217
Die, Ranger Force!

18:13.300 --> 18:17.304
One more left, huh? I can finally go home.

18:17.387 --> 18:20.057
You did pretty well for a lone effort.

18:20.140 --> 18:22.768
Isn't that fighter
the same one from last week?

18:23.268 --> 18:24.269
Last week?

18:24.728 --> 18:27.147
They all look the same,
so I don't remember him.

18:27.856 --> 18:29.775
Now's a good time. Blue!

18:30.609 --> 18:33.237
We'll kill this traitor
with a Divine Artifact.

18:35.697 --> 18:38.158
End him with your Divine Artifact.

18:38.867 --> 18:40.244
Make it look flashy.

18:40.327 --> 18:43.413
Hey, Red!
I want a fight with you!

18:43.497 --> 18:47.501
Red used his Divine Artifact
on some rogue monster the other day.

18:48.001 --> 18:51.421
Getting stuck into a routine is
what we should be worried about the most.

18:52.005 --> 18:56.969
Actually, we've been ending our battles
with random fighters.

18:57.469 --> 18:59.388
Aren't we getting stuck
into a routine here?

18:59.471 --> 19:02.224
Still, we have to get things done.

19:03.016 --> 19:05.144
In that case,
I have a suggestion.

19:05.227 --> 19:08.230
Red. Why don't we change
the plot of the show like this...

19:11.233 --> 19:13.068
It's for the sake of the greater good,
I guess.

19:13.152 --> 19:16.113
Very well. Listen up, monster!

19:16.196 --> 19:18.532
We're impressed by your courage!

19:18.615 --> 19:21.910
It'll be a waste to let someone like you
rot in the Monster Army!

19:21.994 --> 19:23.912
Why don't you surrender
and allow yourself to be captured?

19:23.996 --> 19:25.164
<i>What a surprise!</i>

19:25.247 --> 19:27.332
<i>What a shocking turn of events</i>

19:27.416 --> 19:29.418
<i>in the history of all 13 years
of Sunday Showdown!</i>

19:29.501 --> 19:33.422
Thank your lucky stars.
Don't worry, we'll ensure your safety--

19:33.505 --> 19:35.799
What? I don't want that.

19:36.383 --> 19:37.384
Okay, kill him.

19:41.889 --> 19:43.307
Divine Artifact, Manifest!

19:49.897 --> 19:52.065
<i>This won't end with just my death.</i>

19:52.649 --> 19:54.610
<i>I'm sure someone else will...</i>

19:57.654 --> 19:59.948
It doesn't matter
even if I know we're going to lose.

20:00.532 --> 20:04.077
I'll do my best
to play the perfect monster.

20:08.165 --> 20:09.583
You'll remember me!

20:09.666 --> 20:12.085
Like I said,
I won't be able to remember you.

20:16.798 --> 20:18.467
And it's over!

20:18.550 --> 20:20.761
The Dragon Keepers continue
their victory streak

20:20.844 --> 20:22.262
in this week's Sunday Showdown!

20:22.346 --> 20:24.723
Humanity's peace has been protected!

20:25.307 --> 20:28.727
Yellow! Your hand was covering my face!

20:28.810 --> 20:31.605
You could just learn to adjust, you know.

20:31.688 --> 20:33.732
Come on,
who cares about that?

20:33.815 --> 20:35.275
No need to fight over it!

20:36.068 --> 20:37.694
No, it's important.

20:38.695 --> 20:41.073
We must always appear cool.

20:41.740 --> 20:44.952
Otherwise... we'd look like losers.

20:45.577 --> 20:48.330
Oh, my Divine Artifact is over there.

20:49.790 --> 20:51.917
<i>Still, Pink is right.</i>

20:52.334 --> 20:53.752
<i>We need to reflect on the fact</i>

20:53.835 --> 20:55.921
<i>that we've been ending our fights
with just fighters.</i>

20:58.840 --> 21:03.136
A trash mob is 100 years too early
to be causing trouble for us.

21:06.139 --> 21:07.140
What?

21:07.641 --> 21:08.809
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

21:09.643 --> 21:11.520
<i>That wasn't my Divine Artifact.</i>

21:11.603 --> 21:13.772
<i>It was his left arm!</i>

21:14.648 --> 21:17.109
<i>Where did my Divine Artifact go?</i>

21:20.904 --> 21:22.823
Aww, he died.

21:23.573 --> 21:25.409
You have my thanks, Fighter-kun.

21:25.492 --> 21:27.828
I won't let your sacrifice be in vain.

21:28.704 --> 21:30.247
<i>Now, there's four left.</i>

21:30.330 --> 21:32.833
THE DRAGON KEEPERS

23:04.466 --> 23:07.427
<i>Confirming the situation
based on a reported monster sighting.</i>

23:07.511 --> 23:09.763
<i>Blue Squadron 036! Report in!
Blue Squadron 017, respond!</i>

23:09.846 --> 23:12.015
<i>Blue Squadron 017 and 036!
How's the situation, 017?</i>

23:12.099 --> 23:15.227
<i>What's wrong? 017! 036!</i>

23:29.741 --> 23:31.827
Translated by Qianni Lu

23:31.910 --> 23:33.370
What's wrong, Sakurama?

23:33.453 --> 23:35.956
Suzukiri! Should I eat
<i>yakiniku</i> or <i>omurice?</i>

23:36.039 --> 23:38.792
- This is such a dilemma!
- For goodness sake! You'll have <i>omurice!</i>

23:38.875 --> 23:40.752
Oh! I guess <i>omurice</i> it is, then.

23:40.836 --> 23:42.796
You just accept whatever
people tell you, huh? Well, let's do this!

23:42.879 --> 23:44.339
"The Soldier With Love, Hibiki!"

23:44.423 --> 23:46.842
<i>I'm getting excited!</i>
